.local

# beads: the Dolt DB is the source of truth, backed to the git remote via
# `bd dolt push` (refs/dolt/data); a clone runs `bd bootstrap`. The DB, credential,
# and runtime are handled by beads' own .beads/.gitignore; config.yaml, metadata.json,
# and README.md stay tracked (per beads) so a clone can bootstrap.
# Two intentional overrides of beads' tracked-by-default files:
#   - issues.jsonl: a ~60s-rewritten export — left tracked it churns and is one
#     `git add -A` from looking like the backing. The Dolt ref is the only backing.
#   - interactions.jsonl: an append-only agent-interaction AUDIT log (`bd audit`,
#     for forensics / fine-tuning) — not worth auto-publishing raw agent logs to a
#     public repo, and unused here.
.beads/issues.jsonl
.beads/interactions.jsonl
